sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CV as Controller Volume
    participant CT as Controller
    participant W as Worker
    participant WV as Worker Volume

    rect rgba(100, 149, 237, 0.12)
    Note over CV,CT: Phase 1: Controller startup
    CT-)CV: async read (disk I/O): object metadata
    CV--)CT: object_id, size, ETag, chunk count, per-chunk checksums
    Note over CT: Rebuild object table in memory<br/>Chunk location map starts EMPTY (locations are not persisted)<br/>Enter safe mode: no reads served, no re-replication triggered
    end

    rect rgba(60, 179, 113, 0.12)
    Note over W,WV: Phase 2: Worker startup and registration
    W-)WV: async read (disk I/O): local chunk metadata
    WV--)W: object_id, seq_no, chunk_id, offset, length, checksum
    W->>CT: register (ping): worker_id, address, capacity, free space
    CT-->>W: ACK: registered, heartbeat interval
    W->>CT: full chunk report: list of (object_id, seq_no, chunk_id, checksum)
    Note over CT: For each reported chunk: add W to the replica set of chunk_id<br/>Unknown object_id → mark chunk as orphan<br/>Replica count below replication factor → queue for re-replication
    CT-->>W: ACK chunk report (+ orphan chunk_ids to delete)
    Note over CT: Leave safe mode once reported chunks cover<br/>a threshold of all known chunks (e.g. 99.9%)
    end

    rect rgba(255, 165, 0, 0.12)
    Note over CT,W: Phase 3: Steady state and failure detection
    loop every heartbeat interval (e.g. 3 s)
        alt worker alive
            CT->>W: ping
            W-->>CT: ACK (+ load, free space)
            Note over CT: Reset miss counter, update last_seen
        else no ACK within ping timeout
            CT-xW: ping (lost, no ACK)
            Note over CT: Increment miss counter
            break miss counter reaches N (e.g. 10 misses ≈ 30 s)
                Note over CT: Mark worker DEAD<br/>Remove it from every replica set in the chunk map
                Note over CT: Chunks now below replication factor → re-replication queue<br/>ref: Re-replication sequence (separate diagram)
            end
        end
    end
    end
